  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — specifically, the comparison of the proportion of probability assigned to favorable (non-negative) outcomes — is not present in the verbal report. The individual only notes the low probability of loss, which is a different cognitive focus (risk of loss) than the skewness-based evaluation. The decision reason requires a comparison of favorable versus unfavorable outcomes in terms of probability distribution, which is absent in the report. The individual’s justification does not reference skewness, favorable outcome probabilities, or distributional asymmetry. Therefore, even though the reason is applicable to the problem, the individual did not use it in their reasoning. The verbal report reflects a different decision rationale (low loss probability), not the skewness-based one. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
